WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.580
Controversial tweets, a canceled spin-off,&nbsp;
and an uncertain future in the "Star Wars"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.780
universe. It's finally clear how "The&nbsp;
Mandalorian" is dealing with Cara Dune.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.520
"Star Wars" fans were eagerly awaiting the third&nbsp;
season of "The Mandalorian" for what felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:20.040
the longest time. As viewers geared up for the&nbsp;
latest adventures of Grogu and Din Djarin, one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.380
particular plot thread continued to dangle in the&nbsp;
air, unsolved in the wake of a major controversy.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:32.040
Cara Dune, played by former MMA star and American&nbsp;
Gladiator Gina Carano, was last seen in the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:37.260
season of "The Mandalorian." At the time, Cara&nbsp;
was seen helping rescue Grogu from Moff Gideon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:42.420
played by "Breaking Bad" alum Giancarlo&nbsp;
Esposito. She was slated to continue her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:47.340
work as a marshal for New Republic forces, which&nbsp;
would have lent itself easily to a Dune-centered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:52.080
spin-off. "Rangers of the New Republic," however,&nbsp;
will apparently never see the light of day.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:58.320
Everything changed when Gina Carano was fired by&nbsp;
Lucasfilm in February 2021. The firing happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.060
in the wake of a series of Twitter and Instagram&nbsp;
posts, in which she made controversial statements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:08.820
regarding the COVID-19 pandemic, masking, pronoun&nbsp;
usage, and The Holocaust, among other topics.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.420
"I didn't even know what people were&nbsp;
talking about. I was just not clued in."

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.700
Carano's posts left Dune's fate unresolved,&nbsp;
and fan speculation has run rampant ever since.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.620
Viewers have wondered if the character might&nbsp;
be killed off or recast. Others thought she may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.720
continue to exist in the ether of the larger "Star&nbsp;
Wars" world, alive but never spoken of again.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:33.000
After months of speculation, fans finally have&nbsp;
an answer to their simmering questions. "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.200
Mandalorian" executive producers,&nbsp;
Dave Filoni and Rick Famuyiwa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.880
have spoken out about Dune's status within the&nbsp;
"Mandalorian" world and the "Star Wars" universe.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:47.580
Speaking ahead of the release of "The Mandalorian"&nbsp;
Season 3, Famuyiwa admitted that he and series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:52.620
creator Jon Favreau approached the subject of&nbsp;
Cara Dune's existence carefully, telling Deadline,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:57.000
"Cara was a big part and continues as&nbsp;
a character to be part of the world. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.080
had to be addressed in the creative and [Jon&nbsp;
Favreau] took the time to think about that."

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.460
However, they weren't overly concerned about&nbsp;
the topic of Dune because the show's two central&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.860
characters, Din Djarin and Grogu, are still&nbsp;
in place. As Famuyiwa told the publication,

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.580
"Ultimately it felt like a servicing&nbsp;
of that, and around the Mandalorians."

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.400
When asked about Dune's exact whereabouts in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.040
larger "Star Wars" world,&nbsp;
Dave Filoni told Deadline,

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.960
"It's a big galaxy and we have many characters&nbsp;
in it — many characters are fighting for their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:28.980
screen time. We'll just have to see as the&nbsp;
season unfolds what the adventures are."

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:34.140
Filoni added that Dune was a good character, and&nbsp;
while she was vital to Djarin's formative years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.740
the series is currently concerned with&nbsp;
his growth beyond that period of time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:42.000
So it appears that there are no plans to&nbsp;
revive Dune as a character, but that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.560
will continue to exist in the general cosmic&nbsp;
soup that is the extended "Star Wars" universe.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.560
“I need a marshall.”
“What about Marshal Dune?”&nbsp;

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.719
“After she brought in Moff Gideon,&nbsp;
she was recruited by Special Forces.”

00:02:54.719 --> 00:03:00.180
Filoni also noted that something even more&nbsp;
important is afoot in "The Mandalorian" Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.560
as it will be about the Mandalorian world at&nbsp;
large. The executive producer told Deadline,

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:10.080
"Now Season 3 is mainly dealing with Mandalorians&nbsp;
and the Mandalorian saga, the Mandalorian tale."

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.460
It also appears that Din Djarin's world&nbsp;
will generally be broadened to include a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.500
larger number of people, including people he's&nbsp;
met between adventures, with Filoni teasing,

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.280
"[There are] different characters he's met&nbsp;
since Bo-Katan [who] take a lot more prominence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.720
which makes sense where his arc is going,&nbsp;
the story of him and Grogu specifically."

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.600
When asked if they've gotten&nbsp;
requests to bring Cara Dune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.940
back to "The Mandalorian," Filoni told Deadline,

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:37.680
"I get requests across the board for all&nbsp;
types of characters. I've been with Star Wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.280
it's coming on 20 years. It's a&nbsp;
great galaxy. The hardest thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.560
is finding time and space for everyone out there."

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.940
He added that there are so many characters&nbsp;
battling for screen time within the universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:53.040
but that the purpose of "The Mandalorian" is to&nbsp;
tell the story of Djarin and Grogu. Basically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.720
it would seem that there are no current plans&nbsp;
to use Dune in Season 3. However, it will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:02.460
interesting to see if anything transpires in&nbsp;
a galaxy far, far away in the near future.

